# Rust
/target/
# Cargo.lock is intentionally tracked. This crate builds a `cdylib` WASM
# contract, so the exact dependency graph is part of the build output and must be
# reproducible. It is also load-bearing for correctness: soroban-env-host 22.1.3
# declares `ed25519-dalek = ">=2.0.0"` but calls the 2.x API
# (`SigningKey::generate`), so an unpinned resolve picks 3.0.0 and the build fails
# with E0277 (`ChaCha20Rng: CryptoRng` not satisfied). Pinning 2.2.0 in the
# lockfile is what keeps CI green. The CI cache key also hashes
# `**/Cargo.lock`, which is a no-op while the file is untracked.
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

